---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Front Page
---
<h2 class="headline">City Hall Adopts {{ budgets.latest.fiscalYear }} Budget of {{ budgets.latest.expenditures.total[budgets.latest.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex] | money }}</h2>
<p class="byline">Compiled automatically from the Mayor's {{ budgets.latest.fiscalYear }} Budget, filed with the City Council</p>

<p class="lede">
  The City of Fitchburg adopted a Fiscal Year {{ budgets.latest.fiscalYear }} General Fund budget of
  {{ budgets.latest.expenditures.total[budgets.latest.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex] | money }},
  {% if budgets.prior %}
  {{ budgets.prior.expenditures.total[budgets.prior.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex] | pctChange(budgets.latest.expenditures.total[budgets.latest.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex]) }}
  from the {{ budgets.prior.fiscalYear }} adopted budget of {{ budgets.prior.expenditures.total[budgets.prior.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex] | money }}.
  {% endif %}
  The single largest line remains {{ budgets.departmentTotals[0].name }}, at {{ budgets.departmentTotals[0].value | money }} —
  {{ ((budgets.departmentTotals[0].value / budgets.latest.expenditures.total[budgets.latest.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex]) * 100) | round(1) }}% of the whole budget.
</p>

<div class="stat-grid">
  <div class="stat">
    <span class="value">{{ budgets.latest.expenditures.total[budgets.latest.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex] | moneyShort }}</span>
    <span class="label">FY{{ budgets.latest.fiscalYear }} Adopted Budget</span>
  </div>
  <div class="stat">
    <span class="value">{{ budgets.departmentTotals.length }}</span>
    <span class="label">Budget Lines Tracked</span>
  </div>
  <div class="stat">
    <span class="value">{{ budgets.ok.length }}</span>
    <span class="label">Fiscal Years On Record</span>
  </div>
  <div class="stat">
    <span class="value">{{ documents.financialStatements.documents.length }}</span>
    <span class="label">Audited Statements Archived</span>
  </div>
</div>

{% if summary.fiscalYearsWithLowConfidence and summary.fiscalYearsWithLowConfidence.length %}
<div class="notice">
  <strong>Editor's note:</strong> figures for fiscal year(s) {{ summary.fiscalYearsWithLowConfidence | join(", ") }}
  did not reconcile cleanly during automated extraction and are marked <span class="confidence-low">unverified</span>
  throughout this site pending a manual check against the source PDF. See <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>.
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2 class="section-head">Top Ten Budget Lines, FY{{ budgets.latest.fiscalYear }}</h2>
<table>
  <caption>Adopted General Fund appropriation by department · source: {{ budgets.latest.source.title }}</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Department</th><th>Adopted FY{{ budgets.latest.fiscalYear }}</th><th>Share of Budget</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for d in budgets.departmentTotals | take(10) %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ d.name }}</td>
      <td>{{ d.value | money }}</td>
      <td>{{ ((d.value / budgets.latest.expenditures.total[budgets.latest.expenditures.adoptedColumnIndex]) * 100) | round(1) }}%</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p><a href="/departments/">Read the full department-by-department breakdown, back to FY{{ budgets.ok[0].fiscalYear }} →</a></p>

<div class="pull-quote">
  "The single largest addition to this year's budget was {{ budgets.departmentTotals[0].name }}."
</div>

<h2 class="section-head">Where the Money Comes From</h2>
<p>
  Of the {{ budgets.latestRevenue.revenue.lineItems[budgets.latestRevenue.revenue.lineItems.length - 1].values[budgets.latestRevenue.revenue.adoptedColumnIndex] | money }}
  in operating revenue the city expects to collect in FY{{ budgets.latestRevenue.fiscalYear }}, most comes from local property taxation and state education aid.
  <a href="/revenue/">See the full revenue breakdown →</a>
</p>
